# CODESTREAM-lite — framework source

This directory is the framework's own source, not a project built with it.

`/onboard` and every session's pre-flight must abort when this file is present.
The reason is a one-command trap: the runtime files under `.codestream/` are
tracked by git, so running a single feature through this directory would bake
real project content into every future project that copies it.

Overriding is possible but must be deliberate and session-scoped: state
explicitly that you intend to dogfood the framework here. If a downstream
project ever shows this file, it was copied in by mistake — delete it there;
do not weaken this check.
